---
import Page from "../layouts/page.astro";
import { lastUpdated, operator } from "../operator";
---

<Page title="Terms of Use" description="The rules for using Lardon.">
  <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
  <p class="updated">Last updated {lastUpdated}</p>

  <p>
    These terms apply when you use Lardon, the family cookbook app run by {operator.name}. By
    creating an account or using Lardon, you agree to them. If you don't agree, please don't use
    Lardon.
  </p>

  <h2>Your account</h2>
  <p>
    You need an account to use Lardon. Keep access to your email and your Apple or Google account
    secure, since they're how you sign in. You're responsible for what happens in your account. You
    must be at least 13 years old to use Lardon.
  </p>

  <h2>Your recipes</h2>
  <p>
    You keep ownership of the recipes, photos and other content you add. You give us permission to
    store, process and show that content so Lardon can work, including sharing it with the family
    members you choose. Only add content you have the right to share.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>Don't use Lardon to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>break the law or infringe other people's rights;</li>
    <li>share content that is abusive, hateful or harmful;</li>
    <li>try to access other people's accounts or data;</li>
    <li>disrupt or overload the service, or get around its limits and security.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We may suspend or close accounts that break these rules.</p>

  <h2>The service</h2>
  <p>
    We work to keep Lardon available and your data safe, but we provide it as is and can't promise
    it will always be available or free of errors. Keep your own copies of recipes that matter to
    you. We may change, add or remove features over time.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent the law allows, we aren't liable for indirect losses or for losing content
    because of events outside our reasonable control. Nothing in these terms limits rights you have
    under consumer protection law.
  </p>

  <h2>Closing your account</h2>
  <p>
    You can stop using Lardon at any time and ask us to delete your account by emailing{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${operator.contactEmail}`}>{operator.contactEmail}</a>. See the{" "}
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for what happens to your data.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    If we change these terms, we'll update the date at the top. For important changes, we'll let
    you know in the app before they apply.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by the laws of {operator.country}.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms:{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${operator.contactEmail}`}>{operator.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
